            <ArticleTitle>Coronary arteriography in the presence of dextrocardia and situs inversus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>759-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Given the rarity of dextrocardia, it is not unexpected that there are only a few reports of coronary arteriography in such a setting. We describe a case of successful coronary arteriography in a patient with mirror image dextrocardia and situs inversus, and the technique used, and review the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
